      "ActivityOtherHealthServices": false,
      "ActivityPersuitPurposesDescription": "Seniors Rights Service is a not-for-profit community organisation that has been supporting the rights of older people for 40 years. Our mission is to empower older people to assert their rights through accessible, free and confidential legal services, aged care advocacy and information services across New South Wales. Our role is to advocate for older people, assisting them to claim their rights and support them in exercising those rights so that they enjoy a rich life as seniors and respected members of the community with dignified and equitable access to the care and support they need. In all our endeavours, Seniors Rights Service adheres to principles that empower older people as rights holders, provide high quality and timely services, ensure equitable access for seniors, collaborate with other organisations and work with civil society to foster respect for older individuals and their rights. Seniors Rights Service is an accredited specialist community legal centre that provides assistance to older people in NSW. Our legal service provides free legal advice, casework assistance, information, referral and community legal education. We can advise on matters relating to human rights, planning for the future, consumer rights, retirement living, strata living and boarding house legal advice. Additionally, our aged care advocacy addresses the needs of older people receiving Commonwealth funded aged care services at home and in residential care. We provide targeted rights based information to a diverse range of older people and through information sessions, forums and tailored advice, we continue to serve the diverse needs of our community, striving for a society where older individuals are respected, valued and empowered. We prioritise engagement with older people who are:   disadvantaged and vulnerable   First Nations people   from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds   from the LGBTQ+ community   living in regional, rural and remote locations",
